## 3. Defects found in the server and the bridge (not fixed here; for the sessions on the infrastructure)

1. A read with an id evicts a peer. s-p2p-signal-body (key 65d295215397): when the directory holds more than 63
   entries and the request's id is non-empty and new, s-p2p-evict-one runs before the write is decided; the
   write happens only when there is a payload. So GET /api/p2p/signal?id=X with no msg removes a slot and adds
   nothing. Reading with no id at all neither writes nor evicts.
2. "Evict the oldest" evicts the first listed. s-p2p-evict-one (key bf0e024daa3a) unlinks the head of the
   directory listing; the comment above it says oldest. Inference, not measured: the listing's order is the
   filesystem's, not age.
3. A GET writes presence. s-live-pulse (key 736a54e17cf3) writes /live/<id> on GET, so any crawler or prefetch
   of /api/live/pulse?id=… creates presence. This session created one this way (§1).
4. Figures shown publicly come from fallbacks. cl-bridge-c-4 (key cac27976d010) builds the node heartbeat with
   founder_coinbase_usdc_u6 defaulting to 4325962 and morpho_pool_liquidity_usd_m to 526 when
   /tmp/hx_agent_bus/netpos_maxlev_live.json is absent. The live mailbox on 2026-11-26 showed exactly
   "Base8453 $4.33 settled · $526M 0bp Morpho". Inference: those figures were the fallbacks, not a reading.
5. No TURN. With STUN alone, peers behind symmetric NAT or UDP-blocking networks cannot connect.

## 4. The livestream: what was learned, and why the code was removed

Platform facts, from search on 2026-11-26 (sources: about.instagram.com Live Producer note;
support.restream.io article 18180232; streamyard.com multistream-to-instagram; developers.facebook.com
Live Video API and Instagram live_media reference):

- Instagram has no general API to start a live broadcast. A desktop encoder streams to
  rtmps://live-upload.instagram.com:443/rtmp/<key>, with the key from Live Producer on instagram.com. The key
  is new for every broadcast. Sessions are reported limited to one hour (one source says four). Meta has a
  restricted Live API for eligible accounts, which Restream and StreamYard use and which avoids the
  per-broadcast key. So a continuous Instagram stream is a chain of sessions, each with a new key, unless the
  account qualifies for that API.
- YouTube (rtmp://a.rtmp.youtube.com/live2/<key>) and Twitch (rtmp://live.twitch.tv/app/<key>) keys persist and
  allow 24/7 streaming. Facebook issues its stream URL through POST /<id>/live_videos.
- ffmpeg's tee muxer with onfail=ignore sends one encode to several RTMP(S) targets and drops a failing one
  without stopping the rest. Tested to file only.

The renderer the session wrote (each peer as a 64-bit word drawn as an 8x8 table and a hexagram, sounded at a
pitch from its hexagram, encoded 720x1280 H.264 and AAC) ran and produced valid video. It was removed because
about 26 of its choices were the session's own and not Avik's: the hash (FNV-1a, where the store's identity is
SHA-256), rehashing a peer at each heartbeat, the pentatonic pitch map, every decay, gain, colour and layout
constant, and the encoder settings. By the rules of this repository an agent realizes algorithms Avik states;
it does not supply them. The only result of it worth keeping is the mechanism already in §3.1: a subscriber
that reads with no query never writes to or evicts from the mailbox.

